                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Melbourne FL",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 12 at 9:06PM EDT by NWS Melbourne FL",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nSt Johns River Near Astor affecting Volusia and Lake Counties.\n\n.The St Johns River at Astor remains in Moderate Flood Stage due to\nnorth winds and upstream heavy rainfall draining through the basin.\nRiver levels are forecast to remain near the Moderate Flood Stage\nlevel of 3.0 feet through this week.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Astor...Moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Moderate flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Astor.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 2.8 feet, Docks and boat ramps covered at South Moon\nFish Camp and approaching sea wall at Blair's Jungle Den. Water\napproaching sites closest to the river at Fish Tales RV Resort and\nAstor Landing Campground. Portion of Clair Street covered by river\nwater south of the Butler Boat Ramp. Docks underwater at the Astor\nBridge Marina and along Riveredge Drive. Portions of Fox Road are\ncovered with water nearest to the river. Acorn, Hazelnut and Redbud\nroads are underwater with yards inundated. At 3.0 feet, Water\napproaches or may enter lowest homes on or near Wildhog Road and\nnearby canals. Flooding reaches the parking lot of the Juno Trail\nApartments. Flooding on portions of Alligator Road and Holiday\nRoad. Lowest lying yards along Blue Creek are flooded. Roads at\nAstor Landing Campground and Lake Dexter Boat Ramp begin to flood.\nWater enters lower homes closest to the river on McPherson Lane.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 PM EDT Monday the stage was 3.0 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 2.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 8:30 PM EDT Monday was 3.1 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain steady at around 3.0\nfeet through this week.\n- Flood stage is 2.3 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Tuesday afternoon at noon EDT.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
