                "senderName": "NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 12 at 8:56PM EDT until October 15 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nMyakka River At Myakka River State Park affecting Sarasota County.\n\nWithlacoochee At US 41 Dunnellon affecting Citrus, Levy and Marion\nCounties.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Withlacoochee at US 41 Dunnellon.\n\n* WHEN...Until Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 28.2 feet, Docks and boat ramps flood along the river\nin Citrus and Marion counties.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:45 PM EDT Monday the stage was 28.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 28.2 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 28.2 feet\ntomorrow evening. It will then fall below flood stage early\nThursday afternoon.\n- Flood stage is 28.2 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 28.2\nfeet on 10/02/1979.\n- https://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Tuesday morning at 900 AM EDT.",
